1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
The story of Arthur the Rat. Once upon a time, there was a young rat who couldn't make up his mind.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Whenever the other rats asked him if he would like to come out hunting with them,

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
he would answer in a hoarse voice, I don't know, and when they said,

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
would you rather stay inside, he would say yes or no either.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
He'd always shake making a choice.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
One fine day, his Aunt Josephine said to him,

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
now look here, no one will ever care for you if you carry on like this.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000
You have no more mind of your own than a greasy old blade of grass.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The young rat coughed and looked quiet as usual, but said nothing.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Don't you think so, said his aunt, stamping her foot,

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
for she couldn't bear to see the young rat so cold-blooded.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
I don't know, was all he ever answered.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
And then he walked off to think for an hour or more,

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
whether he would stay in his hole in the ground or go out into the loft.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
One night the rats heard a loud noise in the loft.

16
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
It was a very dreary old place.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The roof let the rain come down, come washing in.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The beams and the rafters had all rotted through,

19
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
so the whole thing was quite unsafe.

20
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
At last one of the joists gave way,

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
and the beams fell with one edge on the floor.

22
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The walls shook, the cupola fell off,

23
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
and all the rats' hair stood on end with fear and horror.

24
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
This won't do, city leader.

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
We can't stay cooped up here any longer.

26
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
So they sent out scouts to search for a new home.

27
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
A little later on that evening the scouts come back

28
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
and said they'd find an old-fashioned art farm,

29
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
where there would be room for all of them.

30
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The leader gave the order at once.

31
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Come new fallen in.

32
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
And the rats crawled out of the hole right away

33
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
and stood on the floor in a long line.

34
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Just then the old rat caught sight of young Arthur.

35
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
That was the name of the shaker.

36
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
He wasn't in the line, and he wasn't exactly outside it.

37
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
He stood just by it.

38
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Come on, get in line, growled the old rat coarsely.

39
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Of course you're coming too.

40
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
I don't know, said Arthur calmly.

41
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Why, the idea of it.

42
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
You don't think it's safe here anymore, do you?

43
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
I'm not certain, said Arthur undaunted.

44
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The roof may not fall down yet.

45
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Well, said the old rat, you can't wait for you to join us.

46
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Then he turned to the other and shouted right about the face.

47
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Marked.

48
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
And the long line marched out the barn while the young rat watched him.

49
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
I think I'll go tomorrow, he said to himself.

50
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
But then again, perhaps I won't.

51
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
It's so nice and snug here.

52
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:18,000
I guess I'll go back to my hole under the log for a while just to make up my mind.

53
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
But during the night there was a big crash.

54
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Down came beams, rafters, joists, the whole business.

55
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Next morning, it was a foggy day, some men came to look over the damage.

56
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
It seemed odd to them that the old building was not haunted by rats.

57
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
But at last one of them happened to move aboard,

58
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:42,000
and he caught sight of a young rat, quite dead, half in and half out of his hole.

59
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Thus the shirker got his due and there was no mourning for him.

